{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1447034-why-would-vampire-vitae-be-banal","id":1447034,"title":"Why would vampire vitae be banal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-02T14:26:03-07:00","id":1447034,"title":"Why would vampire vitae be banal?","content":"So a friend told me that supposedly a changeling suffers banality if they drink vitae from a vampire. I haven't found any reference to it in the rules, but the main question is the philosophy behind it.<br /> <br /> How would drinking vitae cause banality? The extended lore makes it quite clear that vitae is simply quintessence energy stored in blood form. The vampire drains the naturally occurring quintessence from a human through the blood it takes.<br /> The extended lore also makes it clear that glamour is just a refined form of quintessence. Given that, why would vitae be toxic to changelings? Isen't it literally liquid glamour? Im not saying a changeling should be seeking out vampire vitae for easy glamour, because being bloodbound and enslaved by one is not where you wanna be. But why would vitae be antithetical to changeling nature, if it is literally just a different form of the same energy they use?<br /> <br /> Is it because the quintessence/glamour is harvested in a morally incorrect way? That cant be it, since changelings can ravage, and harvest glamour from mortals in equally dickish ways. <br /> <br /> And aren't vampires quite glamorous just be their nature? Terrifying predators of the night, clad in dark auras of unholy magnetism, great seducers and wielding all sorts of fantastical powers. Sure one could make the case that death is inherently banal, but aside from that, vampires are just a evil type of fantasy creature. Thallain and other nightmare creatures aren't banal, even though they also have beastly or evil natures, so why would a vampires be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25428-ebtard","user":"Ebtard","date":". 05-02-2021, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25428-ebtard","name":"Ebtard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T17:33:01-07:00","id":1447061,"title":"","content":"Not a Banality expert, but I expect it comes down to one or two things:<br /> <br /> A) Death. Vampires are Undead, and the deathly nature of Vitae either negates the &quot;vitality&quot;/&quot;energy&quot; of Glamour, or consumes it.<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> B) The Curse. I lean more towards this one, because violence, predation, and darkness have been shown associated with some typed of Glamour. But the Curse of Caine is generally depicted as a tainted and corrupting form of power, and in the case of Glamour it may corrupt it into Banality.<br /> <br /> Of course, it could be that, technically, Vitae doesn't cause actual Banality, but instead causes an almost identical effect despite being a very different cause/source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T18:33:49-07:00","id":1447072,"title":"","content":"My interpretation would be that vampiric vitae would both be a source of Dark Glamour and Banality.<br /> <br /> While vampires are definitely frightening, dreadful, and tortured enough creatures to make them flush with enough Dark Glamour to make any Thallain swoon (and thus make most kithain on edge) I think the other side of the coin is that vampires by their nature are static, unchanging, and stagnant. While it\u2019s less evident in young kindred they\u2019re still metaphysically resilient to change and glamour is almost always inherently dynamic.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s true that vitae is a form of quintessence but imo it shouldn\u2019t be as simple as one size of quint fitting all. Glamour comes in a variety of resonances based upon the nature of its creation and how it\u2019s harnessed. Vitae comes interwoven with the stagnation and sinister resonance which is inherent to the vampiric nature.<br /> <br /> So imo while vitae could be a source of dark glamour, I\u2019d also make it a source of banality. Because I also think the tragedy of a Changeling becoming slowly undone by the addiction brought on by the blood causing them to grow colder and more detached from the Dreaming is suitably poignant and impactful to be solidified into canon through mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T06:30:27-07:00","id":1447183,"title":"","content":"There's also the issue that vampire vitae is effectively the equivalent of heroine or methamphetamines with unhealthy dependent and obsessive relationships thrown in to the mix. Whatever rush it gives you is offset by a number of very terrible side effects. If Changeling is about ideas of artistic creativity, freedom and inspiration (and the torments which sometime come with it), then a Changeling using vampire blood is akin to those artists trapped in a spiral of self-destructive addiction and caring more about their next fix than their art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T06:41:54-07:00","id":1447184,"title":"","content":"If you want a more narrative reason it would be this. Caine, and by extension his progeny, are locked into a set and existent story: rivalry and repetition of the first murder. It is someone else's tale and it is locked in place with no margin for creativity. Any glamour or creativity is drained away by the inexorable flow of this fate. It may not have the same reason for banality as the modern world, but it certainly has reason nonetheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T16:25:24-07:00","id":1447296,"title":"","content":"Drinking vitae leads to the enslavement of the person doing the drinking. The Changeling becomes a thrall to the vampire as a stage towards the blood bond. I'm sure that's part of it. Vampires are also inherently banal (except Malkavians) and vitae is basically the essence of vampirism. As parasites, they're the antithesis of the hopes and wonders of life that the fae are supposed to represent.<br /> <br /> The other posters here also have some very good ideas why. They probably all relate on a metaphysical level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ebtard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1447034-why-would-vampire-vitae-be-banal#post1447034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And aren't vampires quite glamorous just be their nature? Terrifying predators of the night, clad in dark auras of unholy magnetism, great seducers and wielding all sorts of fantastical powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what pro-vampire propaganda wants you to believe. In truth, it's just an excuse to murder you, torment your soul, and lock you into a nightly existence where assuaging your Hunger is the most important thing to you.<br /> <br /> Humans find vampires terrifying because they are our predators. But vampires are actually sad, disgusting, and pitiable creatures. The best possible thing to do for them is destroy them and liberate their souls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YgqgSaDCgC4\" data-code=\"YgqgSaDCgC4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YgqgSaDCgC4/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 05-05-2021, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T21:06:56-07:00","id":1447331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ebtard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1447034-why-would-vampire-vitae-be-banal#post1447034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a friend told me that supposedly a changeling suffers banality if they drink vitae from a vampire. I haven't found any reference to it in the rules, but the main question is the philosophy behind it.<br /> <br /> How would drinking vitae cause banality? The extended lore makes it quite clear that vitae is simply quintessence energy stored in blood form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is not True. Have you looked up what vitae does to mages? There is nothing SIMPLE about Vitae. It has a number of secondary side effects that even the most resonence tainted of Other Tas options do not meet. Particularly Static quintessence by itself is probably an issue for changelings. Vitae is worse than just static resonent quint/tass given how it can litterally addict an avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T15:17:45-07:00","id":1447461,"title":"","content":"It usually is as Vitiae is a thing of stasis and false affection. The opposite of glamour, through some Fae of House Balor have found a way to get blood dross","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T19:10:01-07:00","id":1447511,"title":"","content":"I think, simply put, vampire blood is a spiritual poison. Wherever you think vampirism came from, something really powerful wanted to put his cigarette out using the first vampire\u2019s soul, and it shows from every direction (and splat lens) that vampires are viewed from. Everyone who looks at a vampire knows that they are to be feared, hated, and avoided like you would a plague rat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T18:21:35-07:00","id":1451784,"title":"","content":"Stasis, pure and simple. Glamour is creativity, change, and potential. Vampires have lost the ability to change, which only grows more pronounced with time. Physically, they are 'locked' into one state of being, and over time, their minds also lose the ability to adapt; hence, the Elders who struggle to understand modern technology. <br /> <br /> In short, the state of being a vampire is the antithesis of all that Glamour embodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24663-observer","name":"Observer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}